## A diagram on a slide

A Mermaid flowchart renders inline and follows the deck's light/dark theme.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  A[One .tmd source] --> B{Render}
  B --> C[Page]
  B --> D[Deck]
  B --> E[Book]
```

## Speaker notes

The audience sees the slide; only the presenter sees the notes.

::: {.notes}
This is a speaker note, hidden from the audience view.
:::

## Ask "what if?" live

Change the control and the slide recomputes. The value rides the deep-link, so a
shared address reopens the exact slide *and* this control's state.

{{< input name="rate" type="slider" min="0" max="20" step="1" value="8" label="rate %" >}}

```{js}
//| input: rate
const p = document.createElement("p");
const r = tali.value("rate");
p.textContent = "at " + r + "% growth, 100 becomes " + (100 * (1 + r / 100)).toFixed(1);
return p;
```

# A deeper topic

Right, down, or Space steps into this section's sub-slides in order, the same as
anywhere else in the deck; in the overview they group as their own row.

